" Twilight " director Catherine Hardwicke appeared on "The Kyle Buchanan Show" and weighed in on Robert Pattinson 's buzzy casting as the new James Bond actor. Hardwicke is largely responsible for shooting Pattinson's career into the stratosphere by casting him as the vampire Edward Cullen opposite Kristen Stewart as Bella Swan in 2008's "Twilight." Flash forward nearly 20 years and Pattinson is now set to become the movie's most iconic secret agent. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

"I almost fell out of my bad," Hardwicke said about the moment she found out about Pattinson's Bond casting. "I just didn't think they were going to choose him because of the Batman and he's so famous and they like to get the unknown [actor]. I did almost fall out of the bed, and that is the same bed that Rob and Kristen auditioned for the first time and did their kissing scene. It was kind of bizarre. He fell out of the best and landed on the floor, so it was kind of cool." Related Stories Daniel Radcliffe Is Unsure If He'll Watch HBO’s ‘Harry Potter’ and Says the New Star ‘Doesn’t Need Any Advice From Me’ 'Adolescence' Writer Jack Thorne Adapts Matt Haig’s 'The Humans' for London’s West End With 'House of the Dragon' Star Matt Smith

Hardwicke added, "He's intense and interesting and has got a lot of stuff going on in there. He's weird and he's original. He does not fit the mold. He's not afraid to say crazy shit, that's what I love about it."

Pattinson and Stewart auditioned for "Twilight" together at Hardwicke's home, where the director was interested to see whether or not the actors had the kind of instant chemistry that was required for Edward and Bella.

&#x201C;[Rob] walked in and he had his hair dyed black for some play, with these wacky bangs. He was a bit out of shape. His shirt was just all messy, and I&#x2019;m like, &#x2018;Oh, okay. Okay, let&#x2019;s see how this goes,'&#x201D; Hardwicke told &#x201C;The Big Hit Show&#x201D; podcast in 2022, noting that Pattinson got "so into" the kissing scene with Stewart that he &#x201C;he fell off the bed.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;I&#x2019;m like, &#x2018;Dude, calm down.&#x2019; And I&#x2019;m in there filming with my little video camera, whatever&#x2026;In the end, Kristen was like, &#x2018;It has to be Rob,'&#x201D; the director added. &#x201C;I could tell they had a lot of chemistry, and I&#x2019;m like, &#x2018;Oh my God.&#x2019; I thought, Kristen was 17. I don&#x2019;t want to get in some illegal things. So I remember I told Rob, &#x2018;By the way, Kristen is 17. In our country, it&#x2019;s illegal to have a sexual&#x2026;&#x2019; And he&#x2019;s like, &#x2018;Oh, okay, whatever.'&#x201D;

Stewart remembered the audition while speaking to The New Yorker in 2021, saying: &#x201D;[Pattinson had an] intellectual approach that was combined with &#x2018;I don&#x2019;t give a fuck about this, but I&#x2019;m going to make this sing.&#x2019; And I was, like, &#x2018;Ugh, same.&#x2019; And, whatever, we were young and stupid and, not to say that we made it so much better, but that&#x2019;s what it needed, and that&#x2019;s what anybody playing those parts needed to feel.&#x201D;

When Pattinson's Bond casting was announced earlier this month, "Twilight" fans took to social media to note how the franchise predicted the news. In a scene from Hardwicke's original movie, Justin Chon's character, Eric Yorkie, passes out flyers to his fellow high schoolers and notes this year's prome theme as he announces Forks High School&#x2019;s prom theme is Monte Carlo, adding: &#x201C;Gambling, tuxedos, and Bond. James Bond.&#x201D; The camera that cuts to Pattinson's Edward Cullen. "You probably saw that scene online where we say, 'Bond, James Bond,' and then we cut to Rob. That's the one scene where I was like, 'Let's put the sunglasses on,'" Hardwicke said in her latest interview. "He got out of the car and he looked so suave that he inspired the line, 'Bond, James Bond.' It was cool. We did think he looked like James Bond. I guess we were seeing the future."

Watch Hardwicke's full appearance on "The Kyle Buchanan" show in the video below.

