Chris Evans is returning to the Marvel Cinematic Universe for Avengers: Doomsday despite hinting he was done with the franchise.

Evans' Captain America was written out of the MCU in 2019's Avengers: Endgame , when the superhero passed the baton to Anthony Mackie's Sam Wilson. However, despite Evans saying he was "happily retired" and "sad to not be back with the band," the actor met with Marvel about a&#xA0;potential return.

"He&#x2019;s very committed to saving the experience for the movie theater," director Anthony Russo told Entertainment Weekly . "He&#x2019;s like, &#x2018;Why would we ever compromise that?&#x2019; Of anybody involved, as far as the cast goes, he may be the most committed to that aspect." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

