James was recently seen in Swiped , inspired by Bumble founder Whitney Wolfe Herd, which she also produced through her company Parodos Pictures. Additionally, she recently starred in David Mackenzie&#x2019;s Relay , which debuted at the Tribeca Film Festival and was released theatrically by Bleecker Street.

The Golden Globe nominee's upcoming films include Guy Nattiv&#x2019;s psychological drama The Liberation , set for release in January 2027, Neon and Takashi Miike&#x2019;s Bad Lieutenant: Tokyo , Amazon MGM Studios&#x2019; Subversion , and the Cliffhanger reboot, which she produces for Parados Productions alongside Gala Gordon who co-produces.

James is represented by UTA, Tavistock Wood, and Sloane Weber Offer Dern. Foley is represented by UTA and Cathryn Summerhayes at Curtis Brown Group. Sims is represented by Linden Entertainment and UTA.

In one of the most sweeping, romantic moments of The Other Bennet Sister , Tom Hayward (D&#xF3;nal Finn) recites the poem &#x201C;Composed Upon Westminster Bridge&#x201D; for Mary Bennet (Ella Bruccoleri), Pride & Prejudice 's misfit sibling turned unlikely romantic heroine. The delivery of the poem is wrenching; the scene, in a small rainy garden, idyllic. And yet the scene, adapted by screenwriter Sarah Quintrell from Janice Hadlow&#x2019;s novel of the same name, was scaled back dramatically from how it reads in the book &#x2014; taking place against the splendor of the actual Westminster Bridge. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Lifestyle "Sometimes You Just Have to Think: 'What Will Make People Laugh?'": Lolly Adefope on Gags, 'Ghosts' and Her West End Debut TV NBC to Air Princess of Wales Cancer Charity Documentary

&#x201C;Our budget is a Mary-Bennet-[level], appropriate, ordinary, like-all-of-us sized budget &#x2014; it&#x2019;s not a kind of massive franchise genre-tastic kind of thing. It's humble. We couldn't film on Westminster Bridge &#x2014; we just couldn't afford it,&#x201D; according to Emmy-winning executive producer Jane Tranter ( Succession ). &#x201C;We were cramped into this tiny little garden full of rain&#x2026;to create a scene that just feels so big and so moving and so emotional on very, very little. It's all about text and performance and intent. That is what The Other Bennet Sister is all about. It's not flashy or fancy, with loads of money spent on it. It's about the truth and the emotion.&#x201D;

Audiences have taken note. It&#x2019;s not just the full-house crowd that packed the San Vicente Bungalows on Friday evening to watch select clips from the series &#x2014; and catch Tranter alongside Bruccoleri and Finn in conversation &#x2014; as part of The Hollywood Reporter &#x2019;s exclusive THR Frontrunner screening series. Following its smash initial run in the U.K. on the BBC , The Other Bennet Sister drove unprecedented subscriber growth for North American distributor BritBox and generated wide critical acclaim. The 10-episode series will compete as a limited series this guild season as well as at next year&#x2019;s Primetime Emmy Awards. A three-episode holiday special will air this Christmas. During the panel, the trio discussed key scenes from the original series before teasing the special to come. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The show&#x2019;s main attraction, of course, is Bruccoleri&#x2019;s moving, nuanced turn, which embodies the core idea behind the show &#x2014; that heroes on screen don&#x2019;t always present the way we expect them to. &#x201C;The dialogue seemed rooted in something that you didn't see very often in period drama, where there were awkward overlaps and people saying something that wasn't exactly what they wanted to say and kind of retracting it,&#x201D; says the Wicker star of what appealed to her about the project. &#x201C;I was really excited by seeing that on the page. It felt like I was reading a young woman that could have existed today, that could have existed at any time &#x2014; and it just happened to be set in Regency England. But it felt really relevant to now.&#x201D;

The series centers on the romantic arc between Mary and Tom, who is engaged when they first meet; by the end of the finale, Tom and his previous fianc&#xE9;e have broken things off and he&#x2019;s proposed to Mary. The special is set to explore the beauties and frustrations of their new marital life. &#x201C;There&#x2019;s a beautiful sentiment throughout The Other Bennet Sister , which is about examining societal norms and rules and what is expected of a young person or a young woman &#x2014; how that narrative deserves to be examined and that there are opportunities in many ways to be happy,&#x201D; Finn says. &#x201C;[What] I love about these next three episodes is that there's a further investigation of what it is to be happy in a relationship and to keep a hold of your individuality and to prioritize your systems of living and whether they serve you.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-thr-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setLazyLoadMultiplier(2) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

You can watch the full panel conversation above. The Other Bennet Sister is streaming on BritBox.

Whether it&#x2019;s Alan Cumming starring in a love story about self-acceptance or a lesson in proudly embracing one&#x2019;s cultural background or projects examining the U.S. from an international perspective, these 10 shorts spotlight true humanity and, at times, harsh realities of today's society on screen.

&#x201C;People who are often overlooked have entire stories behind who they are, and we just don't think about it,&#x201D; says writer-director Dolores Rice, whose film opens with Maeve (Liz Fitzgibbon), a shy woman in her 40s, hesitantly discussing weight-loss injections with her doctor. When the physician indicates where the jabs need to go on her body, she recoils and retreats. &#x201C;Up to 46% of women struggling with their weight have been sexually assaulted as children,&#x201D; explains Rice. &#x201C;I wanted to tell the story of overcoming this shame. Breaking this silence with hope seemed urgent and universal.&#x201D; Teenage Maeve (Willow McCarthy) had a life filled with freedom, dance and friendship. How does trauma derail all that? McCarthy also wrote and performed the song that closes the short, &#x201C;Storm,&#x201D; a defiant anthem of strength: &#x201C;Maeve's a dancer, and dancers&#x2019; relationship to music is inherently in their bodies.&#x201D; Rice adds: &#x201C;This embodied reclamation is what the film is dealing with.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories How the ‘Elsinore’ Makeup Team Transformed Stars Andrew Scott and Olivia Colman to Bring the Story of Ian Charleson to Life

&#x201C;&#xA1;Que Suene La Banda!&#x201D;

In U.S. media, &#x201C;you hear a lot of Mariachi, which I love,&#x201D; says director and co-writer Jorge Parra Jr., &#x201C;but Banda&#x2019;s something different.&#x201D; The brass-heavy Mexican music was integral to his childhood in El Monte, California, much as it is a formative part of Javier&#x2019;s (Anthony Gonzalez) family life in &#x201C;&#xA1;Que Suene La Banda!,&#x201C; albeit something he&#x2019;s trying to distance himself from while at school, where his father works as a janitor. &#x201C;Growing up, you try to fit in, right?&#x201D; says Parra. &#x201C;I was a first-generation American. My parents were born in Mexico, and being immersed in the culture in the U.S., you try to pick and choose what you want to show people.&#x201D; Gonzalez calls Parra&#x2019;s film a &#x201C;story that needs to be told&#x201D; and a lesson in not being &#x201C;embarrassed or ashamed of your culture or background, or where your family comes from. Embrace it. It&#x2019;s a beautiful story.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;The catalyst was an actual shooting at my local supermarket,&#x201D; says Nora Arnezeder, the film&#x2019;s French director and co-writer, who felt an urgency to create the short about a child-sitter merely going about her day, with a fateful trip to buy groceries. &#x201C;For a couple of years, I did really have a hard time leaving my home,&#x201D; Arnezeder says, calling the film a &#x201C;very important therapy for me to heal myself.&#x201D; During the entire short, the shooter remains off-screen, a specific choice that gives a non-American perspective on mass shootings in the U.S., according to producer Yoann Scherb. &#x201C;In our society we have a tendency to put the perpetrators in the front,&#x201D; adds Arnezeder. &#x201C;I really needed to focus on the victims.&#x201D;

